pub fn compute_hmac_sha1(key: &[u8], payload: &[u8]) -> [u8; 20] {
    let mut mac = HmacSha1::new_from_slice(key).expect("hmac key any size");
    mac.update(payload);
    let result = mac.finalize().into_bytes();
    let mut out = [0u8; 20];
    out.copy_from_slice(&result);
    out
}
```

Use the `Mac::verify_slice` method which performs a constant-time comparison internally:

```rust
pub fn verify_hmac_sha1(key: &[u8], payload: &[u8], expected: &[u8]) -> bool {
    let mut mac = HmacSha1::new_from_slice(key).expect("hmac key any size");
    mac.update(payload);
    mac.verify_slice(expected).is_ok()
}
```

Never use `==` on raw HMAC bytes for verification; that leaks information through timing side channels. The `subtle` crate's `ConstantTimeEq` is the underlying primitive used here.

