On lookup, check the negative cache before invoking compute. After a failed compute, insert into the negative cache with a short TTL. Be careful: caching errors indefinitely turns transient failures into permanent ones. A common bug pattern in production. Use a max negative TTL of 30-60 seconds and limit cache size to bound memory.

